== Service verification through port-forward ==

$ kubectl port-forward service/webapp 8080:80 -n mzinga-lab4
Forwarding from 127.0.0.1:8080 -> 8080
Forwarding from [::1]:8080 -> 8080

$ curl -s http://localhost:8080/
{"version": "1.0.0", "color": "blue", "hostname": "webapp-5f4f778774-hc6d4", "message": "Hello from version 1.0.0"}

$ curl -s http://localhost:8080/health
{"status": "ok"}

== Step 3 — In-Place Rolling Upgrade (v1 to v2) ==

$ docker build -t mzinga-webapp:2.0.0 .
Successfully built 76745bb6dd
Successfully tagged mzinga-webapp:2.0.0

$ minikube image load mzinga-webapp:2.0.0

$ kubectl set image deployment/webapp webapp=mzinga-webapp:2.0.0 -n mzinga-lab4
deployment.apps/webapp image updated

$ kubectl get pods -n mzinga-lab4
NAME                      READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE
webapp-76745bb6dd-277dj   1/1     Running   0          25s
webapp-76745bb6dd-wm9bd   1/1     Running   0          24s
webapp-76745bb6dd-zzwrk   1/1     Running   0          14s

$ kubectl rollout status deployment/webapp -n mzinga-lab4
deployment "webapp" successfully rolled out

== Service verification during and after Rolling Upgrade ==

# Traffic loop monitoring terminal (Local port 8081)
$ while true; do curl -s http://localhost:8081/ | python3 -c "import sys,json; d=json.loads(sys.stdin.read() or '{}'); print(d.get('version', 'Error'), d.get('hostname', ''))"; sleep 0.5; done
1.0.0 webapp-5f4f778774-hc6d4
1.0.0 webapp-5f4f778774-wsz2c
2.0.0 webapp-76745bb6dd-277dj
1.0.0 webapp-5f4f778774-zth26
2.0.0 webapp-76745bb6dd-wm9bd
2.0.0 webapp-76745bb6dd-zzwrk
2.0.0 webapp-76745bb6dd-277dj

# Observation: Traffic successfully transitioned from version 1.0.0 to version 2.0.0 (green) progressively without any service interruption or downtime (Zero-Downtime Deployment).

== Step 3.5 — Emergency Rollback (v2 to v1) ==

$ kubectl rollout undo deployment/webapp -n mzinga-lab4
deployment.apps/webapp rolled back

$ kubectl rollout status deployment/webapp -n mzinga-lab4
deployment "webapp" successfully rolled back

$ kubectl get pods -n mzinga-lab4
NAME                      READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE
webapp-5f4f778774-5fmhb   1/1     Running   0          78s
webapp-5f4f778774-fdbn5   1/1     Running   0          70s
webapp-5f4f778774-wtq2k   1/1     Running   0          79s

== Service verification after Rollback & Notes ==

# Technical note on port-forwarding:
# After executing the 'rollout undo' command, the internal cluster state successfully reverted to v1 (hash 5f4f778774). The local port-forward tunnel was restarted on port 8081 to correctly refresh the target pod endpoints and clear the stale network sockets.

$ kubectl port-forward svc/webapp 8081:80 -n mzinga-lab4
Forwarding from 127.0.0.1:8081 -> 8080
Forwarding from [::1]:8081 -> 8080
Handling connection for 8081

$ curl -s http://localhost:8081/
{"version": "1.0.0", "color": "blue", "hostname": "webapp-5f4f778774-5fmhb", "message": "Hello from version 1.0.0"}
